    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nIf you set the buftype to `acwrite` it makes it so that read/write events are handled by autocmds. Then, you can use `BufWriteCmd` and `BufReadCmd` to handle simulated read/write events.\r\n\r\nThis way, you could have `:w` from the `mini.files` buffer do the same thing as pressing `=` from the same buffer.",
