        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Oh, that is interesting! I somehow missed the presence of `acwrite` buffer type.\r\n\r\nI don't think this will be a part of 'mini.files'. Here is my current reasoning:\r\n\r\n- Ergonomics. Hitting single `=` is at least not more key presses than anything user can have set up for saving files.\r\n- Code design. Right now there is an action to synchronize all buffers. Allowing \"sync on save\" would mean adding new logic in code. Besides it would mean that not all user edits would be accounted for (like copy and move from another directory).\r\n- Technical details. Saving buffer means using certain approach at adding name to buffer which I don't think I'd like to add, as it increases complexity for not much benefit (together with previous points).\r\n\r\nI think about it and revisit in a couple of days.",
