        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": ">Technical details. Saving buffer means using certain approach at adding name to buffer which I don't think I'd like to add, as it increases complexity for not much benefit (together with previous points).\r\n\r\nWith `buftype=acwrite` it doesn't matter at all what the buffer name is as long as it isn't blank. It just has to have any name, and then your `BufWriteCmd` autocmd handles \"writing\" the buffer, which in this case isn't a file so you don't actually need the buffer name.",
